Native Codex instructions and Python helpers are new work. This package does not
include the upstream Claude hooks, role launcher, permissions or judge runtime.
Imported content has been adapted; it does not establish feature parity.

The shared product contract adapts methods from Michael Jabbour's Worth Using,
Market Fit, Taste × Elegance, Sizzle, Decisioncraft and Right Shape, with file-map
freshness concepts informed by Trail-Code. Exact revisions and adaptation scope
are recorded in upstream.json and references/product.md. Full original MIT
notices are retained in references/sources/*-LICENSE. No external product,
Amplifier runtime, film-production tools or symbol-graph implementation is installed
or bundled by this adaptation.

The command-evidence behavior was also informed by upstream review-run.js and
verify-run.js at revision 3d7c69416dc7524130105c9bfe308aa01b2a26f0 (Delivery
0.37.9). The Python implementation reuses this port's existing raw-byte gates;
it does not import upstream hooks, permissions or role-local mailbox machinery.
